---
title: Charadriiformes
---
# Charadriiformes

Charadriiformes is a large and varied order holding the waders, the gulls, the
terns and the auks of [[alcidae]]. Most members are associated with water,
though habits range from probing an estuary mudflat to years spent entirely at
sea. Several families in the order are among the longest-distance migrants
known.
